.SH NAME
niac-init - Interactive scenario wizard for quick configuration setup


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBniac init [output-file] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Interactive wizard that helps you choose the right scenario and create
a configuration file for your network simulation needs.

.PP
The wizard will ask about your network type, size, and requirements,
then suggest the most appropriate scenario.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for init


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--storage-keep\fP=500
	Run history records to keep, pruned oldest first on start (0 keeps every run)

.PP
\fB--storage-path\fP=""
	Path to NIAC run history database (default: ~/.niac/niac.db)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  # Start interactive wizard
  niac init

  # Start wizard with specific output file
  niac init my-network.yaml

  # Quick workflow
  niac init && niac validate config.yaml
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBniac(1)\fP


